# The abstraction: one resource, two holders, four job states, epochs 1..=4 and
# generations 1..=2. `take_over(e)` is accepted only when `e` strictly exceeds
# the current epoch; a generation advance keeps the epoch and a takeover starts
# generation 1 at the new one.
#
# The four claims checked on every reachable state and every transition:
#   E1 a takeover is accepted only under a strictly greater epoch;
#   E2 no accepted transition lowers the committed epoch;
#   E3 a committed fence never has epoch 0;
#   E4 a takeover installs generation 1 at the new epoch.
#
# Differential conformance drives the real JobQueue with the same steps and
# compares the accept/refuse answer and the observable state (fence, holder,
# released flag, job state) after every step.

